Conclusion: **emit lists and enforces `env_set` as a SECRET sink.**
Check **source** lists it (`c_emit_secret.oo:239`) and the ELF
`check_secret_println_sinks` references `env_set`, but the **product
`check` CLI** type-rejects the unlowered name before the secret walk
reports. Dual-path SECRET is green for **`env_get`** (real op), not for
**`env_set`** (alias / residual name).

`scripts/secret_sink_enforce_smoke.oo` rails `secret_setenv_{fail,pass}`
when present; there is **no** in-tree `secret_env_set_*.oo`. SECRET_TAINT
still says setenv/env_set/unsetenv are **In (partial; re-prove rails)**.

